  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Here line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are parallel.</p><p>So,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0071_43650e2e627a.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 143px;\" /></p><p>Now point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;will satisfy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;so,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Also point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> will satisfy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p><p>Now distance between the&nbsp;parallel line will be the diameter</p><p>Diameter&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>So radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Now mid-point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> will give us centre of circle by symmetry,&nbsp;so by midpoint formula in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> we get centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>Now equation of circle will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"
  }
